---
import ServiceSection from "../components/ServiceSection.astro";
import Endpoint from "../components/Endpoint.astro";
import RustSchema from "../components/RustSchema.astro";
---

<ServiceSection id="service-cache">
  <Fragment slot="title"><code>Cach</code> — cache streams</Fragment>
<p class="endpoint-index"><a href="#cache-get-stream-items-request">Cach/9 request</a><a href="#cache-get-stream-items-response">Cach/9 response</a></p>

    <Endpoint id="cache-get-stream-items-request" direction="client → server" phase="protected bootstrap" structure="generated order" status="live verified">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Cach/9</code> Cache::GetStreamItemsRequest</Fragment>
      <p>Requests items from a named cache stream. Bootstrap requests two localized
      XML catalogs from channel <code>BNET</code>: <code>ERRS</code> for authoritative
      error messages and <code>CONF</code> for public channel names and IDs. Distinct
      request tokens correlate their responses.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`struct GetStreamItemsRequest {
    token: u32,
    generated_check: Bits<23>, // rolling check seeded with 7
    max_items_minus_1: Bits<6>, // requested item count: 1..=50
    stream_kind: bool,          // true = description
    channel: FourCC,
    item_name: FourCC,
    locale: FourCC,
    reference_time: i32,
    direction: bool,            // false = before, true = after
}`} />
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="cache-get-stream-items-response" direction="server → client" phase="protected bootstrap" structure="generated order" status="live verified">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Cach/9</code> Cache::GetStreamItemsResponse</Fragment>
      <RustSchema code={`struct GetStreamItemsResponse {
    items: Vec<CacheStreamItem>, // count: 6 wire bits, 0..=49
    token: u32,
    total_items: u16,
    offset: u16,
}

struct CacheStreamItem {
    _reserved: Reserved<23>,
    // align to the next byte
    content_handle: [u8; 40],
    publication_time: i32,
}`} />
      <p class="endpoint-note">The newest item is selected by publication time. In
      the 40-byte content handle, bytes 0..4 contain an ASCII usage suffix, bytes
      4..8 contain the depot region, and bytes 8..40 contain the content hash. The
      primary URL is
      <code>https://&lt;region&gt;-s2-depot.classic.blizzard.com/&lt;hash&gt;.&lt;usage&gt;</code>.
      A sharded <code>s2-depot-storage</code> URL is the fallback.</p>
      <p>The <code>CONF</code> XML maps public channel IDs to localized names. The
      <code>ERRS</code> XML stores localized messages as
      <code>&lt;e id="code"&gt;message&lt;/e&gt;</code>. Numeric errors from command responses,
      joins, toon creation, and profile operations should use that catalog first,
      with a static symbolic name only as a fallback.</p>
    </Endpoint>
</ServiceSection>
